The number one killer for my 12-conduct attempts is getting separated
from my pet by a trap and then cornered by monsters. How can you
prevent that?

Tactics that help reduce but not eliminate such incidents all depend
on equipment a starting character does not have: Taming all the
domestic animals you meet. Staying within sight of your pet. Keeping
it leashed for when you eventually hit a trap door yourself. Searching
where it whines. Luring monsters to places where they are unlikely to
corner you, especially if you have a key. Carrying escape items, such
as a wands of teleportation, digging, and polymorph; tools to scare
monsters; cursed gain level; or a magic whistle. Throwing the monster
a wand of magic missile so that it shoots itself with the reflection.
A scroll of scare monster plus a stack of holy water is the solution
once you can get it.

Before anybody suggests it: Elbereth, killing the offenders, reading
teleportation, genocide, or a boulder fort would all break conducts.

I would like advice for this typical example. You might want to watch
the last few hundred turns, starting from where my cat fell down the
trapdoor.

